                <pb facs="0630" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg546"/>

                <head>No. 287.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Stallo.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 9,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Stallo is informed by Mr. Bayard that it is his desire that he should attend
                    the conference for the protection of industrial property to be held at Borne on
                    April 29, 1886. He is instructed to state that his presence is merely
                    consultative and wholly <hi rendition="#italic">ad referendum.</hi></p>
            </div>
        </body>
